# ACL-X Runtime

Use this skill only after the current run actually needs reusable ACL-X machine state from `{{RUNTIME_ROOT}}`.

- `t0`: stay in natural language.
- `t1`: one real handoff or shared package -> tiny ACL-X `C-layer` bundle.
- `t2`: reusable machine state -> runtime bridge prompt with `Machine contract`, required artifacts, and acceptance invariants.
- `t3`: repeated loop or resume -> runtime bridge prompt with loop invariants, checkpoint artifacts, and ACL-X resume handles.

Once a run reaches `t2` or `t3`, do not replace machine state with free-text notes. Keep shared artifacts and checkpoint/resume prompts on the runtime bridge.
If the prompt already includes `Machine contract` or `Loop invariants` plus an ACL-X bundle, treat that prompt as sufficient runtime contract and skip rereading ACL-X docs/examples unless blocked.
If a contract-complete `t2` prompt already names the artifact and acceptance checks, do not reread `fixture.json`, `AGENTS.md`, this skill file, or hidden machine-only runtime files unless a required fact is missing.
If a contract-complete `t3` prompt already names the checkpoint and includes an ACL-X bundle, do not reread `fixture.json`, hidden machine-only runtime files, `AGENTS.md`, this skill file, or general skill-creation docs unless a required fact is missing.
For contract-complete `t2/t3` runs, skip plan narration and go straight to edit, verify, and finish unless blocked.
